    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d575">

                <pb facs="0681" n="585" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg585"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Merry to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">San José, Costa Rica</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1899-09-07"><hi rendition="#italic">September
                                7, 1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 310.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to advise that the decree
                    of the Government of Costa Rica, in relation to reciprocity in international
                    copyright, copy and translation of which accompanied my No. 305 of August 30,
                    was published on September 4 in the Official Gazette at this capital, as
                    becoming effective on the 1st of November, 1899.</p>
                <p>With assurances, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Lawrence Merry</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Minister.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
